      "message": "Research brief for a one-word native window (nine positive unknowns)\n\nONE_WORD_WINDOW.md records what the present compiler window is (tableau\nword C, test word F as the cyclic convolution with the temporal shift,\nthe four-block rank and the two mask tests forced by population\nsaturation), proves on paper what the kernel can absorb (quotients, one\nsigned quantity by weight, one positivity by the margin-scale device,\nwhich trades alpha for C but removes nothing) and cannot (two interacting\npositivities), and lists three places where a one-word redesign could\nact, with the repository files to start from. Direction chosen by the\nowner on 24 October 2026; no result is claimed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
